WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.975 --> 00:00:09.975
HQ, module one: leads and customers. How a lead gets from your website to a signed deal without anyone re-keying it.

2
00:00:10.878 --> 00:00:22.963
Every channel lands on one board. Website forms, Colebot chats, Marketplace replies, Messenger, phone calls and walk-ins. The stage columns are the ones a sales floor actually uses.

3
00:00:23.866 --> 00:00:32.135
Open a card and you get the whole story. The ad that produced the lead, the pre-approval stamped to the customer, the unit they want, and every touch, in order.

4
00:00:33.038 --> 00:00:40.300
Text, email or log a call from the card. Messages go out from the store's own local number and land back on the same card.

5
00:00:41.201 --> 00:00:52.460
Now the part that runs while you sleep. Colebot works the website, Messenger and text around the clock. It knows your units, your payments and your programs, and it hands off when it is time.

6
00:00:53.362 --> 00:01:03.486
A customer builds the deal on the unit page. Your rates, your fees, your protection products. A soft-pull pre-approval, then a refundable deposit to hold the unit.

7
00:01:04.388 --> 00:01:14.583
Press hold, and here is what lands in HQ: the lead, the pre-approval, the deposit and a fully structured deal, assigned to a rep, before the store opens.

8
00:01:15.485 --> 00:01:23.387
Back on the board, the card is already in Desking. One click starts the deal with the customer, the unit and the credit carried over.

9
00:01:24.288 --> 00:01:30.435
One record per customer, every channel, every module. That is the CRM in HQ.
